PlotTrellis example data
========================

A small project that renders a first figure with no setup: see ?plottrellis_example.
It covers chr2:103,250,000-103,500,000 (mm10), holding the Ehf, Elf5 and Cat genes, for two
mouse mammary epithelial populations, basal cells (Basal) and luminal progenitors (LP).
Elf5, a luminal progenitor transcription factor, is almost silent in Basal (about 2 TPM)
and highly expressed in LP (about 530 TPM), with the same two main transcripts in both.

Source
------
Milevskiy MJG, Coughlan HD, Kane SR, et al. Three-dimensional genome architecture
coordinates key regulators of lineage specification in mammary epithelial cells. Cell Genomics 2023;
3(11):100424. doi:10.1016/j.xgen.2023.100424. GEO SuperSeries GSE227750.

Files
-----
samples.txt
    The project description PlotTrellis reads (hand-written). Paths in it are relative to
    this folder.

atac/Basal_ATAC.bw, atac/LP_ATAC.bw
    ATAC-seq coverage (RPKM, 50 bp bins), cropped to the region above from the authors' GEO
    files: GSM7142618 (GSM7142618_Ba_S1_ATAC.bw, basal biological replicate 1) and
    GSM7142621 (GSM7142621_LP_S1_ATAC.bw, LP biological replicate 1).

quant/Basal_rep1/quant.sf, quant/LP_rep1/quant.sf
    Salmon transcript quantification (Salmon 2.1.1, GENCODE vM25 index) of RNA-seq runs
    SRR23919859 (basal replicate 1) and SRR23919856 (LP replicate 1) from GSE227748, the
    RNA-seq part of GSE227750, quantified by the PlotTrellis authors from the public reads.
    Only the rows for the transcripts in the GTF below are kept; values are unchanged, so
    TPM does not sum to one million here.

gencode.vM25.example.gtf.gz
    Every GTF line for the 6 genes inside the region, plus the file header, from GENCODE
    mouse release M25 (GRCm38/mm10), gencode.vM25.annotation.gtf.gz.

gencode.vM25.example_chrom_sizes.rds
    mm10 chromosome lengths from UCSC (GenomeInfoDb::Seqinfo(genome = "mm10")), shipped so
    the first launch doesn't need to download them.

Licence and terms
-----------------
- GEO data (the ATAC tracks, and the RNA-seq reads behind the quant.sf files): NCBI places
  no restrictions on the use or distribution of GEO data, though submitters may claim
  patent, copyright or other rights in the data they submitted
  (https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/geo/info/disclaimer.html). Please cite the paper above.
- GENCODE annotation and UCSC chromosome sizes: freely available without restriction.
- The cropping and Salmon quantification are distributed with PlotTrellis under its
  licence (Artistic-2.0).

How it was made
---------------
data-raw/build-example-data.R in the PlotTrellis source repository rebuilds every file here
except samples.txt and this README.
